IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `eia-core-interpretation`
IMPORT `er6-related-provisions`

-- Tests of the Related Provisions. Expected values are written from the text (SOR-96-332.txt lines 2371-2488), not from the rules.
-- The days of royal assent and of coming into force are not in the text; where a test needs one it uses a TEST VALUE, said so in the comment:
-- Thursday 12 March 2009 for the royal assent of 2009, c. 2 (Sunday 1 March 2009 is then the second Sunday before it), and so on.

§ `SOR/2001-495 s 4`

-- "a benefit period established before November 18, 2001"
#ASSERT `Regs related provision SOR/2001-495 s 4 section 77.1 as it read before November 18, 2001 governs the exclusion of low-earning weeks` (YMD 2001 11 17)
#ASSERT NOT (`Regs related provision SOR/2001-495 s 4 section 77.1 as it read before November 18, 2001 governs the exclusion of low-earning weeks` (YMD 2001 11 18))
#ASSERT NOT (`Regs related provision SOR/2001-495 s 4 section 77.1 as it read before November 18, 2001 governs the exclusion of low-earning weeks` (YMD 2020 6 1))

§ `SOR/2002-280 s 2`

-- "benefit periods that commence on or after the day on which these Regulations come into force" (test value for that day: 2002 11 17)
#ASSERT `Regs related provision SOR/2002-280 s 2 the amending Regulations apply to the benefit period` (YMD 2002 11 17) (YMD 2002 11 17)
#ASSERT `Regs related provision SOR/2002-280 s 2 the amending Regulations apply to the benefit period` (YMD 2003 1 5) (YMD 2002 11 17)
#ASSERT NOT (`Regs related provision SOR/2002-280 s 2 the amending Regulations apply to the benefit period` (YMD 2002 11 16) (YMD 2002 11 17))

§ `2009, c. 2, s. 225 -- the second Sunday before royal assent`

-- test value for the royal assent: Thursday 12 March 2009. The Sundays before it are 8 March and 1 March.
#ASSERT `Regs related provision 2009 c 2 s 225 the second Sunday before the day on which the Act receives royal assent` (YMD 2009 3 12) EQUALS YMD 2009 3 1
-- on a Saturday (14 March), a Monday (9 March) and a Sunday (15 March) the same Sundays are before the day
#ASSERT `Regs related provision 2009 c 2 s 225 the second Sunday before the day on which the Act receives royal assent` (YMD 2009 3 14) EQUALS YMD 2009 3 1
#ASSERT `Regs related provision 2009 c 2 s 225 the second Sunday before the day on which the Act receives royal assent` (YMD 2009 3 9) EQUALS YMD 2009 3 1
#ASSERT `Regs related provision 2009 c 2 s 225 the second Sunday before the day on which the Act receives royal assent` (YMD 2009 3 15) EQUALS YMD 2009 3 1
-- on Sunday 8 March the first Sunday before is 1 March and the second is 22 February
#ASSERT `Regs related provision 2009 c 2 s 225 the second Sunday before the day on which the Act receives royal assent` (YMD 2009 3 8) EQUALS YMD 2009 2 22

-- "whose benefit period has not ended before the second Sunday before the day ... and does not begin after September 11, 2010"
-- arguments: a claimant referred to in 55(7); the first day of the benefit period; the last day; the day of royal assent
#ASSERT `Regs related provision 2009 c 2 s 225 Schedule 10 determines the maximum number of weeks` TRUE (YMD 2009 1 4) (YMD 2009 3 1) (YMD 2009 3 12)
#ASSERT NOT (`Regs related provision 2009 c 2 s 225 Schedule 10 determines the maximum number of weeks` TRUE (YMD 2009 1 4) (YMD 2009 2 28) (YMD 2009 3 12))
#ASSERT `Regs related provision 2009 c 2 s 225 Schedule 10 determines the maximum number of weeks` TRUE (YMD 2010 9 11) (YMD 2011 9 10) (YMD 2009 3 12)
#ASSERT NOT (`Regs related provision 2009 c 2 s 225 Schedule 10 determines the maximum number of weeks` TRUE (YMD 2010 9 12) (YMD 2011 9 10) (YMD 2009 3 12))
#ASSERT NOT (`Regs related provision 2009 c 2 s 225 Schedule 10 determines the maximum number of weeks` FALSE (YMD 2009 6 7) (YMD 2010 6 5) (YMD 2009 3 12))
-- the combined rule: the Schedule 10 figure, or NOTHING when the section does not apply
#ASSERT `Regs related provision 2009 c 2 s 225 the maximum number of weeks for which benefits may be paid` TRUE (YMD 2009 6 7) (YMD 2010 6 5) (YMD 2009 3 12) 700 EQUALS JUST 19
#ASSERT `Regs related provision 2009 c 2 s 225 the maximum number of weeks for which benefits may be paid` TRUE (YMD 2009 1 4) (YMD 2009 2 28) (YMD 2009 3 12) 700 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Regs related provision 2009 c 2 s 225 the maximum number of weeks for which benefits may be paid` FALSE (YMD 2009 6 7) (YMD 2010 6 5) (YMD 2009 3 12) 700 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Regs related provision 2009 c 2 s 225 the maximum number of weeks for which benefits may be paid` TRUE (YMD 2009 6 7) (YMD 2010 6 5) (YMD 2009 3 12) 419 EQUALS NOTHING

