§ `2009, c. 30, ss. 3 to 6`

`test years` a b c d e f MEANS `er6 Years of contribution before the benefit period` WITH
    `years among the 10 years before in which the claimant contributed at least 30% of the maximum annual employee’s premium` IS a
    `years among the 11 years before in which the claimant contributed at least 30% of the maximum annual employee’s premium` IS b
    `years among the 12 years before in which the claimant contributed at least 30% of the maximum annual employee’s premium` IS c
    `years among the 13 years before in which the claimant contributed at least 30% of the maximum annual employee’s premium` IS d
    `years among the 14 years before in which the claimant contributed at least 30% of the maximum annual employee’s premium` IS e
    `years among the 15 years before in which the claimant contributed at least 30% of the maximum annual employee’s premium` IS f

-- s 3 applies to "a claimant referred to in subsection 55(7) ... paid less than 36 weeks of regular benefits in the 260 weeks before the beginning of
-- the claimant's benefit period ... established during the period that begins on January 4, 2009 and ends on June 5, 2010"
#ASSERT `Regs related provision 2009 c 30 s 3 the section applies to the claimant` TRUE 35 (YMD 2009 1 4)
#ASSERT `Regs related provision 2009 c 30 s 3 the section applies to the claimant` TRUE 0 (YMD 2010 6 5)
#ASSERT NOT (`Regs related provision 2009 c 30 s 3 the section applies to the claimant` TRUE 36 (YMD 2009 6 1))
#ASSERT NOT (`Regs related provision 2009 c 30 s 3 the section applies to the claimant` TRUE 35 (YMD 2009 1 3))
#ASSERT NOT (`Regs related provision 2009 c 30 s 3 the section applies to the claimant` TRUE 35 (YMD 2010 6 6))
#ASSERT NOT (`Regs related provision 2009 c 30 s 3 the section applies to the claimant` FALSE 35 (YMD 2009 6 1))
-- the increases, paragraph by paragraph: (a) 5 weeks for 7 of the 10 years ... (f) 20 weeks for at least 12 of the 15 years
#ASSERT `Regs related provision 2009 c 30 s 3 the increase in the number of weeks` (`test years` 7 7 7 7 7 7) EQUALS 5
#ASSERT `Regs related provision 2009 c 30 s 3 the increase in the number of weeks` (`test years` 6 7 8 9 10 11) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `Regs related provision 2009 c 30 s 3 the increase in the number of weeks` (`test years` 0 8 0 0 0 0) EQUALS 8
#ASSERT `Regs related provision 2009 c 30 s 3 the increase in the number of weeks` (`test years` 0 0 9 0 0 0) EQUALS 11
#ASSERT `Regs related provision 2009 c 30 s 3 the increase in the number of weeks` (`test years` 0 0 0 10 0 0) EQUALS 14
#ASSERT `Regs related provision 2009 c 30 s 3 the increase in the number of weeks` (`test years` 0 0 0 0 11 0) EQUALS 17
#ASSERT `Regs related provision 2009 c 30 s 3 the increase in the number of weeks` (`test years` 0 0 0 0 0 12) EQUALS 20
#ASSERT `Regs related provision 2009 c 30 s 3 the increase in the number of weeks` (`test years` 0 0 0 0 0 15) EQUALS 20
#ASSERT `Regs related provision 2009 c 30 s 3 the increase in the number of weeks` (`test years` 0 0 0 0 0 11) EQUALS 0
-- when more than one paragraph is met, the largest increase applies (fork F-30-LARGEST): (a) and (c) both met
#ASSERT `Regs related provision 2009 c 30 s 3 the increase in the number of weeks` (`test years` 7 0 9 0 0 0) EQUALS 11
-- the deemed number of weeks: 25 otherwise, increased by 5 for 7 of the 10 years
#ASSERT `Regs related provision 2009 c 30 s 3 the number of weeks of benefits deemed to apply` TRUE 35 (YMD 2009 6 1) (`test years` 7 0 0 0 0 0) 25 EQUALS JUST 30
#ASSERT `Regs related provision 2009 c 30 s 3 the number of weeks of benefits deemed to apply` TRUE 36 (YMD 2009 6 1) (`test years` 7 0 0 0 0 0) 25 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Regs related provision 2009 c 30 s 3 the number of weeks of benefits deemed to apply` TRUE 35 (YMD 2009 6 1) (`test years` 0 0 0 0 0 0) 25 EQUALS JUST 25

-- s 4: benefit periods established June 6, 2010 to July 10, 2010; (a) 3 weeks for 8 of the 11 years ... (e) 15 weeks for at least 12 of the 15 years
#ASSERT `Regs related provision 2009 c 30 s 4 the section applies to the claimant` TRUE 0 (YMD 2010 6 6)
#ASSERT `Regs related provision 2009 c 30 s 4 the section applies to the claimant` TRUE 0 (YMD 2010 7 10)
#ASSERT NOT (`Regs related provision 2009 c 30 s 4 the section applies to the claimant` TRUE 0 (YMD 2010 6 5))
#ASSERT NOT (`Regs related provision 2009 c 30 s 4 the section applies to the claimant` TRUE 0 (YMD 2010 7 11))
#ASSERT `Regs related provision 2009 c 30 s 4 the increase in the number of weeks` (`test years` 10 8 0 0 0 0) EQUALS 3
#ASSERT `Regs related provision 2009 c 30 s 4 the increase in the number of weeks` (`test years` 0 0 9 0 0 0) EQUALS 6
#ASSERT `Regs related provision 2009 c 30 s 4 the increase in the number of weeks` (`test years` 0 0 0 10 0 0) EQUALS 9
#ASSERT `Regs related provision 2009 c 30 s 4 the increase in the number of weeks` (`test years` 0 0 0 0 11 0) EQUALS 12
#ASSERT `Regs related provision 2009 c 30 s 4 the increase in the number of weeks` (`test years` 0 0 0 0 0 12) EQUALS 15
#ASSERT `Regs related provision 2009 c 30 s 4 the increase in the number of weeks` (`test years` 7 7 8 9 10 11) EQUALS 0
-- under s 4 the 10-year count alone gives nothing (paragraph (a) of s 3 has no counterpart)
#ASSERT `Regs related provision 2009 c 30 s 4 the increase in the number of weeks` (`test years` 10 7 0 0 0 0) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `Regs related provision 2009 c 30 s 4 the number of weeks of benefits deemed to apply` TRUE 10 (YMD 2010 6 20) (`test years` 0 0 0 0 0 12) 30 EQUALS JUST 45

-- s 5: benefit periods established July 11, 2010 to August 7, 2010; (a) 1 week for 9 of the 12 years ... (d) 10 weeks for at least 12 of the 15 years
#ASSERT `Regs related provision 2009 c 30 s 5 the section applies to the claimant` TRUE 0 (YMD 2010 7 11)
#ASSERT `Regs related provision 2009 c 30 s 5 the section applies to the claimant` TRUE 0 (YMD 2010 8 7)
#ASSERT NOT (`Regs related provision 2009 c 30 s 5 the section applies to the claimant` TRUE 0 (YMD 2010 7 10))
#ASSERT NOT (`Regs related provision 2009 c 30 s 5 the section applies to the claimant` TRUE 0 (YMD 2010 8 8))
#ASSERT `Regs related provision 2009 c 30 s 5 the increase in the number of weeks` (`test years` 0 0 9 0 0 0) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `Regs related provision 2009 c 30 s 5 the increase in the number of weeks` (`test years` 0 0 0 10 0 0) EQUALS 4
#ASSERT `Regs related provision 2009 c 30 s 5 the increase in the number of weeks` (`test years` 0 0 0 0 11 0) EQUALS 7
#ASSERT `Regs related provision 2009 c 30 s 5 the increase in the number of weeks` (`test years` 0 0 0 0 0 12) EQUALS 10
#ASSERT `Regs related provision 2009 c 30 s 5 the increase in the number of weeks` (`test years` 0 8 8 0 0 0) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `Regs related provision 2009 c 30 s 5 the number of weeks of benefits deemed to apply` TRUE 10 (YMD 2010 7 20) (`test years` 0 0 0 10 0 0) 30 EQUALS JUST 34

-- s 6: benefit periods established August 8, 2010 to September 11, 2010; (a) 2 weeks for 11 of the 14 years; (b) 5 weeks for at least 12 of the 15 years
